in Obsidian write into the right [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]zone of a task block and never split a task from its children. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]Every bob-cli writer and every Obsidian gesture that changes a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]task's status or note settles that note's local structure in the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]same write. That means the local future-schedule Blocked rule, the [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]`## Tasks` status groups, and the badge row. `bob task reconcile` [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]then only does clock-driven and vault-wide work, and the drift [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]numbers prove it.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]13[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]better_o_gesture_settle.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/better_o_gesture_settle.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-q4[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-q4/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Hand-edit mirror never writes across notes[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]mirror-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mirror-guard: fix bead bob-cli-py. Check the debounced dependency and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mention mirrors against the original note path, flush or cancel them [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]when the note changes, stop the baseline cache poisoning, and add a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]regression test that switches notes inside the debounce window.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]o and O open real siblings after the whole subtree[/bold #D7AFFF]            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]open-lines[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]open-lines: `o`/`O` on task headlines open a fresh `#task \\[created::]` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]after the whole block. Inside a status group they open at the intake [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]end. Reqs, drawers, and notes get siblings after their subtree, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]managed lines redirect to the owner's note slot. Empty scaffolds prune [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]themselves, `Ctrl+Shift+]` refuses managed lines, and the coordination [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]note goes on bob-cli-ph.7.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]One pure Rust settle_note that reconcile composes[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]settle-core[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]settle-core: extract reconcile's note-local subset (the local [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]future-schedule Blocked rule plus status groups and badges for eligible [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes) as a pure `settle_note` with a line map. Reconcile composes it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with byte-identical output. Add a writer helper and Rust-owned settle [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vectors for the plugin twin.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Reconcile drift meter and recorded baseline[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]drift-meter[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]drift-meter: add `scripts/dev/reconcile-drift`, which replays vault [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commits through `bob task reconcile --dry-run -f json` with `BOB_NOW` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pinned. It sorts the planned changes into churn categories, attributes [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]them to gestures, and reports tidy debt. Record today's baseline on the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]phase bead.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Plain split and BLOCKS placement match the layout contract[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]layout-parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mirror-guard[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]layout-parity: fix bead bob-cli-pn so plain Task Split writes LINKED [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]FROM in the managed-link zone, update the SP vectors, and re-copy them [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]into the nav split twin. Verify and fix the known JS [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]BLOCKS-before-Depends-On insert-order divergence from contract §14.5.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Capture settles every note it touches[/bold #D7AFFF]                         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]capture-settle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after settle-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]capture-settle: run `settle_note` at the capture choke point after type [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agreement and before the trackers finish. Forward the task-block tracker[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and `items[].result.line` through the line map so dry-run and commit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stay byte-identical and Mac Capture's Open lands on the post-settle [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]line, with no Swift changes.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Task commands and sync writers settle their notes[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]command-settle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after settle-core, layout-parity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]command-settle: compose the settle helper into `bob task move`, `split`,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`merge`, and `restore`, `bob gmail sync`, `bob ref create`, `bob gkeep [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]pull`, and any other status- or residence-changing bob-cli writer the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]audit finds, with fixture proof that a later reconcile plans nothing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]note-local.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Vector-pinned JS settle twin behind a ledger-tools API[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]settle-twin[dim] · [dim][/dim]after settle-core[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]settle-twin: port `settle_note` to bob-ledger-tools, pinned byte for [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]byte by copied settle vectors. Expose it as a versioned `taskSettle` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]API: pure settle, editor apply with a path guard and the cursor policy, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and the tier-2 pending scheduler with a global flush. Consumers degrade [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]to reconcile-heals when the API is absent.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Cycler gestures settle, including recurring spawns and cycling[bold white on #D75F87][/bold #D7AFFF] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler-settle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after settle-twin, open-lines[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler-settle: tier-1 settle on Ctrl+Enter close, which also flips a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]future-scheduled recurring spawn from `[ ]` to `[?]`. Tier-1 settle also[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]covers transcluded completion, promote and demote, and the `o`/`O` [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]scaffold commit. `Alt+]`/`Alt+[` cycling settles on idle and flushes on [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cursor-leave, note-leave, or the next Bob command.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Navigation gestures settle both notes they write[/bold #D7AFFF]             [bold white on #D75F87] large  [/bold white on #D75F87]\n    [#AF87FF]nav-settle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after settle-twin, layout-parity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nav-settle: tier-1 settle on Alt+N, Alt+X, the Task, Decay, schedule, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and priority cards, Ctrl+Shift+M and Task Split (source and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]destination), and status-changing mirror writes. Walk rows, recorded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]jumps, and focus targets resolve by identity after the regroup, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]every nav command flushes pending settles first.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Link and Pomodoro target writes settle their target notes[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]link-settle[dim] · [dim][/dim]after settle-twin[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]link-settle: tier-1 settle on block-id-prompt's Ctrl+Shift+Enter target [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]writes and on ledger-tools Pomodoro close and other target-note status [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]writes, in the same write and including notes not open in an editor.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Ctrl+Shift+O opens a note where note_home says[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]notes-key[dim] · [dim][/dim]after open-lines, cycler-settle[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]notes-key: after bob-cli-ph.7, `Ctrl+Shift+O` opens a note at the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]owner's note slot through the shared drawer helpers. That is the tail on[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]zero-req tasks, the Notes drawer on req owners (created only when a note[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]lands), and `## Notes` on a `^prj`. `- [` typed below notes or drawers [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]re-slots into the reqs zone with the first-req scoop.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]End-to-end settle acceptance and re-measure[/bold #D7AFFF]                  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]acceptance[dim] · [dim][/dim]after mirror-guard, open-lines, settle-core, drift-meter, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]layout-parity, capture-settle, command-settle, settle-twin, [/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#AF87FF][dim]cycler-settle, nav-settle, link-settle, notes-key[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]acceptance: a fixture-level end-to-end suite where every wired gesture [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and writer leaves reconcile with nothing note-local to plan and tidy at [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]zero. It runs the drift meter over post-deploy vault history against the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]baseline and does a final docs sweep. With approval, it also writes the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]settle decisions record.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-q4","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-q4.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-27f445333495f2ef13c37760b59c7b02","started_at":"2026-11-25T13:53:46.075966+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"fc4d504dd84bf190bfad21752312812dc3879ffc8878a9879817035d7ccafa68","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-q4.6/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"286be244cdacd51e7a3f316f6ea7faef8acc984e5fe03954ce2b5795aafc57f6","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-q4.6/meta.json","size_bytes":688},"prompt":{"digest":"6b5e8ee7e319a8ebd59d33acf07fe82b6acdd10314533ffe2fc9d100b8fd02a8","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-q4.6/prompt.md","size_bytes":176},"state":{"digest":"cb87323271932ade94d47a014cd41e48c100ea4c4b145983b873661dd6245114","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-q4.6/state.json","size_bytes":163}},"finished_at":null,"global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-q4.6","local_name":"bob-cli-q4.6","metadata":{"agent_clan":"bob-cli-q4","agent_clan_generation":"20261125085248","bead_id":"bob-cli-q4.6","changespec_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","cl_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_